  "goodToKnow": "Die Schlucht is a gorge or ravine: eine tiefe Schlucht. In the Alps, a narrow gorge is often called eine Klamm, like the Partnachklamm near Garmisch-Partenkirchen or the Breitachklamm. Das Tal is a valley. The Wutachschlucht in the Black Forest is a well-known hiking gorge. Related to schlucken (to swallow). Plural: die Schluchten."
